; Under +spad-vector-memory a vector spill slot is never reloaded by a scalar
; load: the vector spill wrote every lane's copy of the slot into the
; scratchpad, and a scalar load, which takes no lane offset, would read one
; lane's copy. Without the feature InlineSpiller folds the reload of a
; vfmv.f.s source into flw/fld (getFoldedOpcode); with it the slot is
; reloaded whole and vfmv.f.s reads element 0. The vmv.x.s fold (lw/ld) is
; refused the same way but not pinned: whether vmv.x.s may be used is a
; register file question.
;
; RUN: llc -mtriple=riscv64 -mattr=+v,+spad-vector-memory \
; RUN:   -riscv-v-vector-bits-max=128 -verify-machineinstrs < %s \
; RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,SPAD
; RUN: llc -mtriple=riscv64 -mattr=+v \
; RUN:   -verify-machineinstrs < %s | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,STD

